{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1851","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Lisa and the Martians"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lisa was kidnapped by martians! It okay, because she has watched a lot of TV shows about aliens, so she knows what awaits her. Let's call integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a non-negative integer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"strictly less than"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2^k$$$, for example, when $$$k = 12$$$, the numbers $$$51$$$, $$$1960$$$, $$$0$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the numbers $$$\\pi$$$, $$$-1$$$, $$$\\frac{21}{8}$$$, $$$4096$$$ are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The aliens will give Lisa $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. Then they will ask her to name any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number $$$x$$$. After that, Lisa will select a pair of numbers $$$a_i, a_j$$$ ($$$i \\neq j$$$) in the given sequence and count $$$(a_i \\oplus x) \\& (a_j \\oplus x)$$$. The operation $$$\\oplus$$$ means "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://tiny.cc/xor_wiki"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bitwise exclusive OR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", the operation $$$\\&$$$ means "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://tiny.cc/and_wiki "},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bitwise And"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, $$$(5 \\oplus 17) \\& (23 \\oplus 17) = (00101_2 \\oplus 10001_2) \\& (10111_2 \\oplus 10001_2) = 10100_2 \\& 00110_2 = 00100_2 = 4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lisa is sure that the higher the calculated value, the higher her chances of returning home. Help the girl choose such $$$i, j, x$$$ that maximize the calculated value."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — number of testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each testcase is described by two lines."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integers $$$n, k$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le 30$$$) — the length of the sequence of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers and the value of $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\lt 2^k$$$) — a sequence of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"martian"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all testcases "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"does not exceed"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, print three integers $$$i, j, x$$$ ($$$1 \\le i, j \\le n$$$, $$$i \\neq j$$$, $$$0 \\le x \\lt 2^k$$$). The value of $$$(a_i \\oplus x) \\& (a_j \\oplus x)$$$ should be the maximum possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are several solutions, you can print any one."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n5 4\n3 9 1 4 13\n3 1\n1 0 1\n6 12\n144 1580 1024 100 9 13\n4 3\n7 3 0 4\n3 2\n0 0 1\n2 4\n12 2\n9 4\n6 14 9 4 4 4 5 10 2\n2 1\n1 0\n2 4\n11 4\n9 4\n2 11 10 1 6 9 11 0 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1 3 14\n1 3 0\n5 6 4082\n2 3 7\n1 2 3\n1 2 15\n4 5 11\n1 2 0\n1 2 0\n2 7 4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First testcase: $$$(3 \\oplus 14) \\& (1 \\oplus 14) = (0011_2 \\oplus 1110_2) \\& (0001_2 \\oplus 1110_2) = 1101_2 = 1101_2 \\& 1111_2 = 1101_2 = 13$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Second testcase: $$$(1 \\oplus 0) \\& (1 \\oplus 0) = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Third testcase: $$$(9 \\oplus 4082) \\& (13 \\oplus 4082) = 4091$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fourth testcase: $$$(3 \\oplus 7) \\& (0 \\oplus 7) = 4$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1851F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1851/problem/F"}